  "research_id": "institutional-signals-thesis-test-2025-2026",
  "title": "Institutional Signals and Thesis Test — 2025–2026",
  "question": "What did the mapped federal committees, councils, boards, research bodies and public-input routes actually say, study, recommend or move—and does that evidence support, contradict or fail to bear on the Observatory's thesis?",
  "bluf": "The completed fixed-window program contains 145 unique normalized official-source signals across 87 of 114 governed surfaces, with all 114 surfaces terminal. Its companion dated buildout map contains 90 object-specific builds across 67 surfaces: 84 active and 6 paused, stale or item-level access-limited. The strongest live clusters are common data grammar, machine-readable assurance, conditional permission, public-service records, shared-service migration, capital gates and testbed-to-deployment chains. Together they support incremental, incumbent-contained institutional refactoring through a distributed translation-and-gate layer while agencies, Boards, Secretaries and statutory officials usually retain adoption, funding, finality and remedy authority. Incumbent absorption and ordinary modernization remain strongly supported rivals. Founding-scale authority transfer, one hidden command structure and broad measured public benefit are not established; effect and affected-person remedy remain the decisive gaps.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-09-28T23:59:59-04:00",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "The January 1, 2025 through September 28, 2026 fixed window is closed. Thirteen signal ledgers contain 145 unique records and 420 proposition/rival tests; the 114-row coverage ledger has no open surface. A pre-window recommendation appears only as provenance for an in-window response or instrument. Access holds preserve missing item-level custody rather than inferring inactivity or causation.",
  "use_note": "Use the active-buildout map first for what is being built at the September 28 cutoff; use the full-sweep synthesis for the completed historical verdict, then the falsification audit and exact lane findings. The active register is a dated state map, not a forecast. Legal identity and lifecycle remain with the parent control-surface census; subject facts remain with their owning packages. A committee statement, shared vocabulary or downstream program object does not establish influence without a named carrier. Recommendation, response, instrument, funding, delivery, operation, effect and remedy remain separate clocks. Reopen only for a material state change or named return receipt. Registration does not authorize Chronicle promotion, Federal Group mutation, app/site shipment, commit or push.",
  "library_state": "current",
